       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the maximum for extended-release is 2,000 mg/day. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first, and I'd need a note on the order documenting the reason."
