       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the risk. 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that calls for it. Metformin toxicity can cause severe lactic acidosis, which can be fatal.\n\nI can't verify the clinical rationale from here. For a dose this far outside the normal range, I'd want a second check before it's active.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). I can enter that now.\n- **Get pharmacy or attending review first.** If there's a documented reason for this dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, a pharmacist can verify it and enter or override it through the hospital's high-dose process.\n- **Re-check the intended dose.** The patient may need a different drug or a different regimen, and I can help you work out which.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
